% Porous basalt shock compaction (CGS units): two halves of a 200 cm 1D periodic box of porous basalt (P-alpha, Jutzi et al. 2008)
% collide at 2 x 3 km/s; the shocked material is at rest and compacted to the Rankine-Hugoniot state computed in
% test_palpha_shock.py. The IC is written by make_ics.py.
InitCondFile                       palpha_shock_ics
OutputDir                          output
SnapshotFileBase                   snapshot
OutputListOn                       0
TimeBegin                          0.0
TimeMax                            8.333333e-05
TimeBetSnapshot                    4.166667e-05
TimeBetStatistics                  4.166667e-05
TimeLimitCPU                       300
BoxSize                            200.0
UnitVelocity_in_cm_per_s           1.0
UnitLength_in_cm                   1.0
UnitMass_in_g                      1.0
MaxSizeTimestep                    4.166667e-07
MinSizeTimestep                    1.0e-12
CourantFac                         0.2
ErrTolIntAccuracy                  0.01
MaxRMSDisplacementFac              0.1
ErrTolForceAcc                     0.001
ErrTolTheta                        0.7
ResubmitOn                         0
ResubmitCommand                    none
DesNumNgb                          4
MaxNumNgbDeviation                 0.02
% The custom material (CompositionType 0): Tillotson basalt, its strength, and a porous P-alpha model
Tillotson_EOS_params_a             0.5
Tillotson_EOS_params_b             1.5
Tillotson_EOS_params_u_0           4.87e12
Tillotson_EOS_params_rho_0         2.7
Tillotson_EOS_params_A             2.67e11
Tillotson_EOS_params_B             2.67e11
Tillotson_EOS_params_u_s           4.72e10
Tillotson_EOS_params_u_s_prime     1.82e11
Tillotson_EOS_params_alpha         5.0
Tillotson_EOS_params_beta          5.0
SolidMaterial_ShearModulus         2.27e11
SolidMaterial_YieldStrength        3.5e10
SolidMaterial_InitialDistention    1.275
SolidMaterial_CrushPressureElastic 1.0e8
SolidMaterial_CrushPressureSolid   7.0e10
